# CITATION.cff — citation metadata for the AI Safety repository.
#
# Notes on honesty: no DOI is asserted (the repository is not a published
# release with a registered DOI); no institutional affiliation is invented;
# the author identity is the repository owner's GitHub account identity.
# Adjust `version` and `date-released` when cutting a real release.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this curriculum or its code supports your work, please cite the
  repository. See research/research-method.md for how its sources are
  verified, and cite the primary sources it points to for technical claims.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdilShamim8/AI-Safety"
title: AI Safety
abstract: >-
  An open-source research curriculum and working project repository covering
  AI safety, alignment, AI security, and evaluations: 24 chapter units,
  10 deterministic runnable projects with honest execution status, 24
  paper/comparison notes, 3 production incident reviews, 22 verified
  dataset cards, a from-scratch researcher track, an annotated resource
  index, and a source/claims register (164 sources, 153 claims) behind
  every number — plus a generated dashboard (index.html) presenting the
  whole build with its evidence ladder.
authors:
  - family-names: Shamim
    given-names: Adil
    website: "https://github.com/AdilShamim8"
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - ai-alignment
  - ai-security
  - ai-evaluations
  - interpretability
  - red-teaming
  - curriculum
license: MIT
license-experimental:
  - name: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
